# (1.5.0, format 37) the project in the frame store, the WORK object: saved there (never OBJ_PROJ again), read at the
# boot; a save while playing goes into a frame erased ahead (no erase: no gap), and when none is left, it waits for the
# stop (autosave); a 1.4 save made since (a return to 1.4.x) taken again at the boot, their newer edits winning; after a
# failed boot the version before; a power cut in a save: the version before; names on the screens and to the reader,
# kept by a save; and mutated WORKs written as the newest version, booted: never half taken (fuzzboot)
wait 300
# (a fresh unit's first boot saved WORK once: the flag of the sets the FM-1 comes with, stored with it)
expect works 1
expect objseq 0
expect format 37
# a change, saved (GLO held) while it plays: into one of the two frames the boot erased ahead
tap ENV
spin K2 -100
spin K2 40
expect par111 40
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
expect dirty 0
expect store_writes 4
expect works 2
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 40
expect format 37
expect migrated 0
workcheck
# mutated WORKs as the newest version, a boot each: the mutated one only when it reads whole, else the one before
fuzzboot 300
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 40
workcheck
# two more saves while playing (a reboot erased two frames ahead again), then a third: none erased, so not yet (no
# erase while playing: a gap); stopped and quiet, autosave saves it
tap ENV
spin K2 5
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
expect dirty 0
spin K2 5
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
expect dirty 0
expect par111 50
spin K2 5
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
expect dirty 1
expect playing 1
tap PLAY
wait 50
expect playing 0
wait 60000
expect dirty 0
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 55
workcheck
# after a failed boot (the guard's count 1): the version before (50), said; then a good boot: the newest again
listen
bootfail
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 50
said OLDER SAVE LOADED
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 55
# a power cut in a save (at its third erase or program): the version before
tap ENV
spin K2 10
expect par111 65
tap PLAY
wait 50
powercut 3
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
expect dirty 1
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 55
workcheck
# names, as a set gives them (the host's "name"): on the screens (the header's tag), to the reader, kept by a save.
# (step 5, Decisions 3) On USB power the battery shows, but steps aside for a name wider than 68 px (WWWWWWW: 84)
usbpower 1
name 2 Night Bus
name 5 WWWWWWW
name -1 Winter Set
expectname 2 Night Bus
expectname 3 Fog
turn PRESET 2
wait 600
expect piece 2
said Night Bus
shot name_header.png
wait 1500
expect hdrbatt 1
shot name_batt.png
turn PRESET 3
wait 600
expect piece 5
shot name_wide.png
wait 1500
expect hdrbatt 0
expect hdrcut 0
shot name_tag.png
usbpower 0
# (Decisions 4) a low battery (under 20%) is never hidden: beside the wide name it shows, the name cut ("…"); charged
# (or none), the name whole and no battery; a name that fits beside it not cut
battery 530
wait 600
expect hdrbatt 1
expect hdrcut 1
shot name_lowbatt.png
battery 600
wait 600
expect hdrbatt 0
expect hdrcut 0
battery 530
turn PRESET -3
wait 2200
expect piece 2
expect hdrbatt 1
expect hdrcut 0
shot name_lowbatt_fits.png
turn PRESET 3
wait 2200
expect piece 5
battery -1
tap PLAY
wait 50
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
expect dirty 0
reboot
wait 300
expectname 2 Night Bus
expectname 5 WWWWWWW
expectname 0 Basic
workcheck
name 5 -
expectname 5 Night Drive
# a 1.4 save made since WORK took the last (a return to 1.4.x, saved there: 36, OBJ_PROJ): taken at the boot, its
# edits winning, and WORK saved from it at once; 1.4's save itself never written by 1.5.0
tap ENV
spin K2 -100
spin K2 20
store36
expect objseq 1
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 20
expect migrated 1
expectname 2 Steppers
workcheck
tap ENV
spin K2 3
tap PLAY
wait 50
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
reboot
wait 300
expect par111 23
expect objseq 1
expect migrated 1
# a .dub1 file (tests/host/work-1.5.0.dub1: a WORK the simulator wrote, names, Fog playing) read as WORK is at a boot:
# (step 4) refused, its "Dub Chamber" (79 px) wider than the header's tag held; (step 5, Decisions 3: the battery steps
# aside, 87 px) read again. The same with "Woodward Dub" (92 px, tests/host/work-1.5.0-wide.dub1) refused; with "Dub
# Room" and slot 5 holding recipe 8's piece (tests/host/work-1.5.0-step4.dub1) read
dub1in tests/host/work-1.5.0.dub1
expect piece 3
expectname 1 Dub Chamber
expectname 6 Pressure 2
expectname 2 Steppers
dub1no tests/host/work-1.5.0-wide.dub1
dub1in tests/host/work-1.5.0-step4.dub1
expect piece 3
expectname 1 Dub Room
expectname 6 Pressure 2
expectname 2 Steppers
expect recipe4 7
expectname 4 Haze
